What: the build neither needs nor links Metal: configure stops requiring metal/metallib,
  libawt, libawt_lwawt, libsplashscreen and libosxui stop linking Metal.framework, the
  java2d/metal native sources are left out of libawt_lwawt, and shaders.metallib is not built.
Why on 10.9: Metal.framework arrived in 10.11, so a library linking it does not load on 10.9.
  Upstream builds all of java.desktop on macOS even headless (--enable-headless-only is refused
  there), and libawt is loaded headless for images and fonts.
Provenance: Hiker159/jdk-macos-legacy@70d25ea1d6f7292c8e926e9efe112f949800ae10, patches/25/mavericks.patch,
  make/autoconf/toolchain.m4 hunk 1/1, make/modules/java.desktop/lib/AwtLibraries.gmk
  hunks 1-4/4, make/modules/java.desktop/lib/ClientLibraries.gmk hunks 1-3/3, unchanged.
Exit: never (no Metal on 10.9).

